    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Job’s Third Speech: A Response to Bildad"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then Job spoke again:"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Yes, I know all this is true in principle.",
          "But how can a person be declared innocent in God’s sight?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If someone wanted to take God to court,",
          "would it be possible to answer him even once in a thousand times?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For God is so wise and so mighty.",
          "Who has ever challenged him successfully?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Without warning, he moves the mountains,",
          "overturning them in his anger."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He shakes the earth from its place,",
          "and its foundations tremble."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If he commands it, the sun won’t rise",
          "and the stars won’t shine."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He alone has spread out the heavens",
          "and marches on the waves of the sea."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He made all the stars—the Bear and Orion,",
          "the Pleiades and the constellations of the southern sky."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He does great things too marvelous to understand.",
          "He performs countless miracles."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Yet when he comes near, I cannot see him.",
          "When he moves by, I do not see him go."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If he snatches someone in death, who can stop him?",
          "Who dares to ask, ‘What are you doing?’"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "And God does not restrain his anger.",
          "Even the monsters of the sea are crushed beneath his feet."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“So who am I, that I should try to answer God",
          "or even reason with him?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Even if I were right, I would have no defense.",
          "I could only plead for mercy."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "And even if I summoned him and he responded,",
          "I’m not sure he would listen to me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "For he attacks me with a storm",
          "and repeatedly wounds me without cause."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He will not let me catch my breath,",
          "but fills me instead with bitter sorrows."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If it’s a question of strength, he’s the strong one.",
          "If it’s a matter of justice, who dares to summon him to court?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Though I am innocent, my own mouth would pronounce me guilty.",
          "Though I am blameless, it would prove me wicked."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“I am innocent,",
          "but it makes no difference to me—",
          "I despise my life."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Innocent or wicked, it is all the same to God.",
          "That’s why I say, ‘He destroys both the blameless and the wicked.’"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "When a plague sweeps through,",
          "he laughs at the death of the innocent."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The whole earth is in the hands of the wicked,",
          "and God blinds the eyes of the judges.",
          "If he’s not the one who does it, who is?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“My life passes more swiftly than a runner.",
          "It flees away without a glimpse of happiness."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          26
        ],
        "lines": [
          "It disappears like a swift papyrus boat,",
          "like an eagle swooping down on its prey."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          27
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If I decided to forget my complaints,",
          "to put away my sad face and be cheerful,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          28
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I would still dread all the pain,",
          "for I know you will not find me innocent, O God."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          29
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Whatever happens, I will be found guilty.",
          "So what’s the use of trying?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          30
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Even if I were to wash myself with soap",
          "and clean my hands with lye,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          31
        ],
        "lines": [
          "you would plunge me into a muddy ditch,",
          "and my own filthy clothing would hate me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          32
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“God is not a mortal like me,",
          "so I cannot argue with him or take him to trial."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          33
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If only there were a mediator between us,",
          "someone who could bring us together."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          34
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The mediator could make God stop beating me,",
          "and I would no longer live in terror of his punishment."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          35
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then I could speak to him without fear,",
          "but I cannot do that in my own strength."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": [],
        "np": true
      }
    ]
  },
